  "reason": "Evidence: scvi_n200 (0.520) outperforms pca_n2000 (0.485) in singleprofile RNA-only, and image-only (resnet50) is weak (0.208), suggesting RNA is the primary signal. Key uncertainty: whether multiprofile aggregation provides meaningful gains over singleprofile, which is a major structural axis affecting ~40 of the 51 configurations. This experiment (scvi_n200 + multiprofile + avgpool) tests that question using the best-known RNA encoder and the simplest aggregation, isolating the profile/aggregation effect with a single logical change from config_004. If multiprofile helps, it justifies investing in transformer aggregation and multimodal multiprofile variants; if it does not, it prunes a large portion of the search space. This is the highest-information-per-experiment choice given the sparse 3-experiment history."
}

